A command with two init functions in one file, which share one reference, each
holding a dead store. The directive above the second binds the second, so it
withholds only the second's store, and the first's is reported.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/app

go 1.27
-- deadset.json --
{"target": {"kind": "application"}}
-- main.go --
package main

func main() {}

func init() {
	v := 1
	v = 2
	_ = v
}

//deadset:ignore DS1404 -- kept for the loader
func init() {
	w := 1
	w = 2
	_ = w
}
